WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.920
The school Saturday requires supraglottic airways and suction as well as CPAP and capnography. This practical lesson joins those skills to the assessment you already learned; it is not another isolated list of devices.
学校周六要求学习声门上气道、吸引、CPAP和二氧化碳监测。本实训把这些技能接回已经学过的评估，而不是再列一份互不相连的器械清单。

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:26.088
We will follow one problem: can air move through the upper airway and produce an adequate breath? Equipment is useful only when it solves that problem without creating a more serious one.
我们始终追问同一个问题：空气能否通过上气道，形成足够的有效呼吸？器械只有在解决问题且不制造更严重问题时才有价值。

00:00:26.088 --> 00:00:39.456
Prepare oxygen, a functioning suction unit, an appropriate bag and mask, adjuncts, monitoring and a backup plan. Assign one person to watch the patient while another prepares the next step.
准备氧气、可正常工作的吸引器、合适的球囊面罩、辅助通气道、监测及后备方案。一人准备下一步时，要明确另一人持续观察患者。

00:00:39.456 --> 00:00:54.024
The explanation prepares you for supervised mannequin practice. The actual school device, current procedure and instructor assessment determine the skill sign-off; no procedure should be practised on an unconsenting person.
本讲解用于准备有督导的模型训练。技能签核必须依据学校实际器械、当前操作规程及教师评估，不能在未经同意的人身上练习操作。

00:00:54.024 --> 00:01:07.872
Responsiveness, breathing and circulation determine the immediate pathway. Gasping is not normal breathing. A trained pulse check must be brief and must not become an excuse for prolonged inaction.
反应、呼吸与循环决定即时处置路径。濒死喘息不是正常呼吸。受训人员查脉搏必须简短，不能因反复找脉而迟迟不行动。

00:01:07.872 --> 00:01:20.496
With a definite pulse but ineffective or absent breathing, open and clear the airway and support breaths. Oxygen through a mask alone cannot replace missing alveolar ventilation.
明确有脉搏但呼吸无效或停止时，应开放并清理气道、支持通气。单纯通过面罩给氧，不能代替缺失的肺泡通气。

00:01:20.496 --> 00:01:34.752
When no definite pulse is found promptly in an unresponsive adult with abnormal breathing, use the arrest pathway and bring an AED. Do not wait to see whether naloxone or a higher oxygen flow will restore circulation.
无反应且呼吸异常的成人，若迅速检查后仍不能确定有脉搏，就进入心搏骤停路径并取得AED。不能等待纳洛酮或更大氧流量恢复循环。

00:01:34.752 --> 00:01:46.368
A suspected foreign body creates a different problem. Forcing a supraglottic device past an obstruction does not remove that obstruction and may delay the intervention that is actually needed.
疑似异物属于不同问题。强行把声门上装置推进阻塞气道，不能移除异物，还可能延误真正需要的处理。

00:01:46.368 --> 00:01:58.392
This is the adult BLS bridge, not the full Week Five resuscitation class. Activate help, begin high-quality compressions and use an AED promptly when arrest is recognized.
这里是成人BLS衔接，不是第5周完整复苏课程。识别心搏骤停后，应启动支援、开始高质量按压并尽早使用AED。

00:01:58.392 --> 00:02:13.152
Compress the lower half of the sternum at one hundred to one hundred twenty per minute, with adult depth about five to six centimetres, full recoil and minimal interruptions. Follow the current trained protocol and feedback device.
在胸骨下半部以每分钟100至120次按压，成人深度约5至6厘米，充分回弹并尽量减少中断；按当前训练方案及反馈装置执行。

00:02:13.152 --> 00:02:26.904
Before an advanced airway, the standard adult BLS ratio is thirty compressions to two breaths. Give breaths that produce visible chest rise rather than two maximal squeezes. Keep the pause short.
未建立高级气道前，标准成人BLS比例为30次按压配2次通气。每次以可见胸廓起伏为目标，不是把球囊挤到底，并应缩短暂停时间。

00:02:26.904 --> 00:02:40.512
Clear everyone for AED analysis and shock, then resume compressions as directed. Assign airway preparation to another rescuer so that searching for equipment does not stop the lifesaving work already under way.
AED分析与放电时须让所有人离开接触点，随后按指示恢复按压。让另一名救援者准备气道，不能因找器械而停止已经开展的救命措施。

00:02:40.512 --> 00:02:53.424
An effective cough and the ability to speak indicate some airflow. Encourage coughing and monitor for deterioration rather than immediately interrupting a useful cough with thrusts or a blind finger sweep.
有效咳嗽及能够说话，说明仍有一定气流。应鼓励咳嗽并监测恶化，而不是立刻用冲击或盲目手指清扫打断有效咳嗽。

00:02:53.424 --> 00:03:07.848
For severe responsive adult or child choking, the current AHA sequence starts with five back blows followed by five abdominal thrusts. Use chest thrusts for late pregnancy or when the abdomen cannot be encircled.
对仍有反应的成人或儿童严重窒息，当前AHA顺序是先5次背部拍击，再5次腹部冲击。妊娠后期或不能环抱腹部时使用胸部冲击。

00:03:07.848 --> 00:03:20.904
An infant uses back blows and chest thrusts, never abdominal thrusts. Support the infant as demonstrated in the current pediatric class; do not copy adult hand placement onto a small infant.
婴儿使用背部拍击与胸部冲击，绝不使用腹部冲击。应按当前儿科课程示范支托婴儿，不能把成人手位直接照搬到婴儿身上。

00:03:20.904 --> 00:03:37.968
The saved June examination guide accepts alternating two effective techniques in sets of five for responsive adults and children. Keep that named examination wording separate from the current AHA starting sequence; ask the instructor which version governs the school station.
存档6月考试指南允许对有反应的成人及儿童，把两种有效技术各5次交替使用。应把这份考试文本与当前AHA起始顺序分开标明，由教师确认学校训练站采用的版本。

00:03:37.968 --> 00:03:52.320
When a responsive choking patient collapses, support the person to a safe surface, activate help and begin CPR with compressions. The collapse branch is not a reason to spend time repeating abdominal thrusts on the floor.
仍有反应的窒息患者倒下时，应扶至安全平面、启动支援，并从胸外按压开始CPR。进入倒地分支后，不能继续在地面反复腹部冲击而耽误复苏。

00:03:52.320 --> 00:04:04.416
Each time the airway is opened for breaths, inspect the mouth. Remove an object only when it is visible and can be reached safely. A blind sweep can push it deeper or injure tissue.
每次开放气道准备通气时，应查看口腔。只有看见并能安全取出的异物才移除；盲目清扫可能将异物推得更深或造成组织损伤。

00:04:04.416 --> 00:04:23.016
The saved examination guide also gives a separate unwitnessed-unconscious obstruction branch: one breath, reposition and another attempt if no entry, then compressions when ventilation remains blocked. Do not confuse that branch with a witnessed conscious-to-unconscious collapse.
存档考试指南另有“发现时已经无意识”的梗阻分支：尝试一次通气，无气流时重新摆位再试，仍受阻则按压。不要把它与目击患者由清醒转为无意识的分支混为一谈。

00:04:23.016 --> 00:04:39.480
Continue reassessment after an object is expelled. Persistent stridor, pain, ineffective breathing or reduced consciousness still requires support and urgent assessment; removal of the visible object is not proof that all danger has ended.
异物排出后仍须继续复评。持续喘鸣、疼痛、呼吸无效或意识下降，仍需支持及紧急评估；取出看见的异物不证明危险全部解除。

00:04:39.480 --> 00:04:52.512
Loss of muscle tone lets upper-airway structures narrow the passage. Snoring may improve when the mandible is lifted; simply pressing a mask onto the face does not correct that internal obstruction.
肌张力丧失可使上气道结构塌陷、通道变窄。抬起下颌可能改善鼾声；单纯把面罩压在脸上，不能解决内部阻塞。

00:04:52.512 --> 00:05:08.496
Use the jaw and head-positioning techniques taught for the clinical situation. With suspected cervical injury, start with a jaw thrust and spinal precautions, but do not accept a closed airway merely to keep an ineffective position unchanged.
按临床情境使用所教的下颌及头部摆位技术。疑颈椎伤时先下颌前移并保护脊柱，但不能为了维持一个无效姿势而接受气道持续闭塞。

00:05:08.496 --> 00:05:21.744
Body habitus can require support beneath the head and upper torso rather than one thin pillow under the occiput. The useful position is the one that improves access and airflow within injury precautions.
体型可能要求同时垫高头部及上躯干，而不是仅在后枕放薄枕。有效体位应在伤情防护范围内改善操作空间及气流。

00:05:21.744 --> 00:05:37.056
After any repositioning, check the result. If chest rise remains absent, reassess the passage, secretions, seal, obstruction and equipment instead of assuming that correct-looking posture guarantees ventilation.
每次调整体位后都要核查结果。胸廓仍不起伏时，应重新检查通道、分泌物、密合、异物及器械，不能假设姿势看起来正确就一定有效。

00:05:37.056 --> 00:05:50.040
A suction unit in its bag is not yet ready. During the equipment check, inspect its power, collection chamber, tubing, connectors and catheter, then test function using the manufacturer method.
吸引器放在袋子里不等于已经可用。器械检查应核电源、收集罐、管路、接头及吸引头，再按制造商方法测试功能。

00:05:50.040 --> 00:06:05.040
A rigid oral tip provides controlled access to visible pooled fluid. A soft catheter has different uses and depth limits; it is not automatically an invitation to advance into a nose, trachea or gastric channel.
硬质口腔吸引头便于受控清除可见积液。软管的用途及深度限制不同，不能因为有软管，就随意伸入鼻腔、气管或胃通道。

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:19.296
Choose vacuum settings for the actual patient, procedure and equipment. A value printed for one specialized i-gel procedure is not the universal setting for every oral, pediatric or tracheal suction task.
负压设置取决于患者、操作及器械。某项i-gel专门流程所列的压力值，不是所有口腔、儿科或气管吸引的通用设置。

00:06:19.296 --> 00:06:33.624
Place the operating suction within reach at the head and prepare ventilation support before beginning. Use the current infection precautions for secretion exposure; gloves alone do not protect eyes and airways from splashes.
开始前应把已能工作的吸引器放在头侧可及处，同时备好通气支持。按当前分泌物暴露防护要求操作，手套不能保护眼睛及呼吸道免受飞溅。

00:06:33.624 --> 00:06:46.608
Wet gurgling and visible fluid suggest contamination that can obstruct airflow or be aspirated. Open the mouth, inspect and use the oral suction technique demonstrated with the actual catheter.
湿性咕噜声及可见液体，提示污染物可能阻塞气流或被误吸。开放口腔、观察，并用实际吸引头按教师示范的口腔技术清理。

00:06:46.608 --> 00:06:59.760
Follow the catheter-specific insertion depth and activation method. Do not sweep blindly into the back of the throat, lever on the teeth or repeatedly traumatize tissue in search of a perfectly dry mouth.
按具体吸引头的置入深度及启动方法操作。不能盲目扫入咽后部、借牙齿作杠杆，或为追求口腔完全干燥而反复损伤组织。

00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:10.944
If a solid object is visible, use the appropriate trained removal method. A small blocked suction opening cannot be repaired by pushing the catheter farther into the patient.
看见固体异物时，应使用适当的受训移除方法。吸引孔被堵，并不能靠把吸引头继续推进患者体内解决。

00:07:10.944 --> 00:07:25.920
Restore oxygenation and ventilation promptly after clearing. With ongoing large-volume contamination, coordinate patient positioning, repeated clearance and additional help rather than alternating long periods with no effective breaths.
清理后要尽快恢复氧合和通气。持续大量污染时，应协调体位、反复清理及额外支援，而不是让患者在长时间没有有效呼吸的状态间来回循环。

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:41.448
Nancy gives maximum oral suction attempts of fifteen seconds for an adult, ten for a child and five for an infant. Do not keep suction on until that clock expires when the airway has already cleared or the patient is deteriorating.
Nancy所列口腔吸引单次最长时间为成人15秒、儿童10秒、婴儿5秒。这是上限；气道已清或患者恶化时，不能为凑满时间继续吸引。

00:07:41.448 --> 00:07:55.800
Suction interrupts oxygen delivery and can trigger gagging, trauma or a vagal response. Stop and reassess when the patient shows harm, and restore required oxygenation and ventilation between attempts.
吸引会打断供氧，并可能引起作呕、创伤或迷走神经反应。出现伤害迹象时应停止并重评，两次尝试之间恢复所需氧合与通气。

00:07:55.800 --> 00:08:08.664
If the unit stops collecting fluid, distinguish a clear airway from a clogged catheter, full canister, leak or power failure. Check the patient first and the entire suction path second.
不再收集液体时，应区分是气道已经清理，还是吸引头堵塞、罐满、漏气或供电故障。先检查患者，再检查整条吸引路径。

00:08:08.664 --> 00:08:22.488
These oral timing figures are not copied into every specialized procedure. The i-gel port method is a separately specified, depth-limited pharyngeal technique, not unrestricted continuous suction.
这些口腔时间数值不能照搬到每一种专门操作。i-gel通道方法是另有规定、限制深度的咽部吸引，不是可以持续开启的无限制吸引。

00:08:22.488 --> 00:08:32.688
The oropharyngeal airway holds the tongue away from the posterior passage. It does not ventilate, seal the larynx or protect the patient from aspiration.
口咽通气道使舌头离开后方通道，但它不会主动通气、不会密封喉口，也不能防止误吸。

00:08:32.688 --> 00:08:43.320
Use it in an unresponsive patient who does not have a gag response and tolerates insertion. Do not deliberately provoke a deep gag to prove that an airway is safe.
用于无反应、无咽反射反应且能够耐受置入的患者。不能故意深刺激咽部，企图证明某种气道操作安全。

00:08:43.320 --> 00:08:57.768
An airway that is too short, too long or poorly placed can worsen obstruction. Measure the selected device and use the demonstrated technique; the adult rotation method is not automatically appropriate for an infant or child.
通气道过短、过长或位置不当，都可能加重梗阻。应测量所选器械并使用所示范的方法；成人旋转置入法不能自动用于婴儿或儿童。

00:08:57.768 --> 00:09:09.168
Reassess airflow and a test breath after placement while maintaining positioning. Remove it if gagging or vomiting occurs, clear the airway and choose another appropriate means of support.
置入后继续维持体位，并通过气流及测试通气复评。若出现作呕或呕吐，应取出、清理气道，再选择适当支持方法。

00:09:09.168 --> 00:09:21.744
A nasopharyngeal airway can be useful when an adjunct is needed but an oral airway cannot be tolerated or placed. It still does not prevent aspiration or remove the need for manual jaw support.
需要辅助通气道但不能耐受或无法放入口咽通气道时，鼻咽通气道可能适用。但它仍不能防止误吸，也不能代替手法下颌支持。

00:09:21.744 --> 00:09:34.704
Current PR zero seven measures the candidate in its neutral curve from nostril to tragus. The textbook offers other landmarks; name the actual procedure rather than silently mixing the methods.
当前PR07要求保持器械自然弯曲，从鼻孔量至耳屏。教材还提供其他标志点，学习时要说明采用哪份规程，不能悄悄混合方法。

00:09:34.704 --> 00:09:46.560
Lubricate the outside without blocking the lumen and advance gently backward along the nasal passage, not upward toward the bridge of the nose. Stop rather than forcing resistance.
润滑器械外侧而不堵内腔，沿鼻道向后轻柔推进，不是向鼻梁上方顶。遇阻应停，不可强推。

00:09:46.560 --> 00:10:01.176
Significant maxillofacial injury, particularly a Le Fort pattern, is an exclusion in the current procedure. Inspect the actual injury and choose an appropriate alternative rather than relying on a little-finger size shortcut.
当前规程将显著颌面伤，尤其Le Fort型骨折，列为禁用情况。应检查实际伤情并选适当替代，不能仅靠“小指一样粗”这样的捷径。

00:10:01.176 --> 00:10:11.424
A flange resting at the nostril proves only that the proximal end is there. Check whether snoring, airflow and ventilation have actually improved.
挡片停在鼻孔，只证明近端到达那里。还要核查鼾声、气流及通气是否真正改善。

00:10:11.424 --> 00:10:26.496
Epistaxis can introduce new airway contamination. Current PR zero seven permits leaving the device if it is not causing compromise; if it obstructs or compromises the airway, remove it and use protective support.
鼻出血可能造成新的气道污染。当前PR07允许在没有造成损害时保留器械；若其引起梗阻或气道受损，则应取出并给予保护性支持。

00:10:26.496 --> 00:10:41.448
The older textbook describes suction through a nasal airway. Current BCEHS PR zero seven explicitly prohibits PCP suction through its lumen. Treat this as a source correction, not as an optional style preference.
旧教材描述了经鼻咽通气道吸引，但当前BCEHS PR07明确禁止PCP经其内腔吸引。这属于来源修正，不是任选一种操作风格。

00:10:41.448 --> 00:10:51.504
After repositioning or transfer, repeat the patient-based check. An adjunct can move or become obstructed even while its flange appears unchanged.
调整体位或转移患者后，应重复患者端检查。即使挡片外观看起来不变，通气道也可能移位或堵塞。

00:10:51.504 --> 00:11:05.064
Check the bag, patient valve, mask, reservoir and oxygen connection as one system. A reservoir full of oxygen does not help when the patient valve is obstructed or the mask is disconnected.
把球囊、患者阀、面罩、储氧袋及氧气连接作为一个系统检查。患者阀堵塞或面罩断开时，储氧袋再满也不能帮助患者。

00:11:05.064 --> 00:11:20.616
Use the appropriate equipment size and manufacturer assembly. The actual oxygen concentration depends on flow, reservoir, seal and patient demand; a fifteen-litre setting is not proof of exactly one hundred percent delivery.
使用适当尺寸及制造商规定的组装方式。实际吸入氧浓度受流量、储氧、密合及患者需求影响，设为每分钟15升不证明精确送入100%氧。

00:11:20.616 --> 00:11:33.840
Add the required compatible filter and capnography connector without creating a kink, unapproved arrangement or excessive dead space for a small patient. Equipment compatibility is part of preparation.
使用要求的相容滤器及二氧化碳采样接头，避免打折、未经批准的组合，或对小患者造成过大死腔。相容性本身就是准备的一部分。

00:11:33.840 --> 00:11:46.752
Test the system before it is urgently needed and keep suction accessible. In a real failure, quickly restore an effective backup instead of repeatedly squeezing an assembly you have not verified.
在紧急需要前测试系统，并使吸引器保持可及。真正失效时应迅速恢复有效后备支持，不能反复挤压一套尚未核实的装置。

00:11:46.752 --> 00:11:59.712
One rescuer must otherwise open the airway, hold a seal and squeeze the bag with only two hands. Two-provider technique separates those jobs and makes failure easier to recognize and correct.
单人只有两只手，却要同时开放气道、维持密合及挤压球囊。双人技术把任务分开，也更容易发现及纠正失败。

00:11:59.712 --> 00:12:12.648
The person at the head supports the mandible with a practiced two-hand grip and holds the mask over nose and mouth. Lift the jaw toward the mask rather than crushing the mask downward into soft tissue.
头侧人员用练熟的双手姿势支持下颌，把面罩覆盖口鼻。应将下颌抬向面罩，而不是向下把面罩压进软组织。

00:12:12.648 --> 00:12:25.584
The second person gives a controlled breath while watching the exposed chest. State whether there is slight definite rise, a leak, resistance or no effect so that the head provider can adjust immediately.
第二人进行受控通气，同时看暴露的胸廓。要明确说出是轻微但清楚的起伏、漏气、阻力，还是完全无效，使头侧人员能立即调整。

00:12:25.584 --> 00:12:36.984
Avoid pressure over the eyes or beneath the chin that closes the passage. A louder squeak or stronger bag squeeze is not proof that a poor mask seal has been corrected.
避免压眼或挤压颏下软组织而闭塞通道。更响的漏气声或更用力挤球囊，都不能证明面罩密合已经改善。

00:12:36.984 --> 00:12:50.928
A breath needs enough volume to expand the chest, not enough to empty an adult bag. Nancy contains a complete-squeeze instruction in its skill drill; do not adopt that wording as a universal volume target.
一次通气需要足以使胸廓扩张的气量，而不是把成人球囊挤空。Nancy的操作表有“完全挤压”字样，不能把它作为普遍通气量目标。

00:12:50.928 --> 00:13:03.288
Give the breath smoothly over about one second in the named BLS framework and watch for slight definite chest rise. Then release pressure and allow the chest to fall before the next breath.
在所指BLS框架中，应约用1秒平稳送入，观察轻微而清楚的胸廓起伏，然后放松压力，让胸廓下降后再给下一次。

00:13:03.288 --> 00:13:17.304
Fast or excessive breaths increase airway pressure, gastric inflation and regurgitation risk. Positive pressure can also reduce venous return, especially in a patient who is already poorly perfused.
过快或过大的通气会增加气道压力、胃胀气及返流风险。正压还可能减少静脉回流，灌注已经不足的患者尤其容易受影响。

00:13:17.304 --> 00:13:28.056
Use the least pressure and volume that achieve the clinical goal. If the chest does not rise, troubleshoot the reason rather than automatically squeezing harder and faster.
应使用达到临床目标所需的最低有效压力及气量。胸廓不起伏时要排查原因，而不是自动更用力、更快速地挤压。

00:13:28.056 --> 00:13:40.776
Look at the patient with every breath. Similar chest rise on both sides, air movement and appropriate resistance give immediate feedback, while abnormal asymmetry requires reassessment.
每次通气都要观察患者。双侧相近的胸廓起伏、气流及适当阻力提供即时反馈；出现异常不对称，应重新评估。

00:13:40.776 --> 00:13:53.160
Pulse oximetry can lag and may initially look reassuring despite poor ventilation. Do not wait for saturation to fall before correcting absent chest rise or a blocked passage.
脉搏血氧可能滞后，通气已经很差时，读数起初仍可能令人放心。不能等血氧下降才处理胸廓不起伏或通道堵塞。

00:13:53.160 --> 00:14:08.496
Capnography adds information about exhaled carbon dioxide, but a low value also depends on perfusion, leak and sampling. Interpret the waveform with chest movement and the clinical state, not as an isolated green number.
呼气末二氧化碳增加了呼出二氧化碳的信息，但低值也受灌注、漏气及采样影响。应把波形与胸廓运动及临床状态一起解释，不能只看一个绿色数字。

00:14:08.496 --> 00:14:20.904
Recheck immediately after moving the head, adding an adjunct, transferring the patient or changing providers. An effective breath five minutes ago does not certify the breath being given now.
移动头部、添加通气道、转移患者或更换操作者后都应立即复查。5分钟前有效的通气，不能证明现在这一次仍然有效。

00:14:20.904 --> 00:14:33.144
When the chest does not rise, announce ineffective ventilation and request help. Reopen the airway, clear contamination and correct the seal while another rescuer checks the connected system.
胸廓不起伏时，要明确宣布通气无效并求援。重新开放气道、清除污染及纠正密合，同时让另一人检查连接系统。

00:14:33.144 --> 00:14:48.672
If there is almost no bag resistance with an audible leak, focus on the interface and disconnected components. If resistance is unexpectedly high, consider obstruction, device blockage and patient causes without forcing pressure.
球囊几乎无阻力且明显漏气时，重点查界面及断开的部件。阻力异常高时，应考虑气道或器械堵塞及患者原因，不能强行加压。

00:14:48.672 --> 00:15:01.872
A correctly placed adjunct can help functional obstruction, but a foreign body or pathology must follow its own pathway. A supraglottic device is not a cure for every cause of difficult bagging.
合适通气道可能改善功能性阻塞，但异物或病理性梗阻必须进入相应路径。声门上装置不能解决所有难以球囊通气的原因。

00:15:01.872 --> 00:15:14.016
Restore the best effective basic support and obtain advanced help when needed. Do not keep repeating a failed maneuver because the next station on the school schedule happens to be SGA insertion.
应恢复当前最有效的基础支持，并按需取得高级支援。不能因为学校下一站刚好教声门上装置，就不断重复一个已经失败的动作。

00:15:14.016 --> 00:15:28.296
The current adult BLS respiratory-arrest rate is one breath every six seconds, or ten per minute, with a definite pulse. The older textbook adult range is not silently relabelled as that same recommendation.
当前成人BLS在明确有脉搏的呼吸骤停分支中，使用每6秒1次，即每分钟10次。不能把旧教材成人范围悄悄改称为同一建议。

00:15:28.296 --> 00:15:42.960
For infants and children with a pulse but absent or inadequate breathing, current AHA and AAP use twenty to thirty breaths per minute. This is not the older twelve-to-twenty range, and newborn resuscitation is a separate framework.
对于有脉搏但呼吸停止或不足的婴儿与儿童，当前AHA及AAP使用每分钟20至30次。这不是旧版的12至20次，新生儿复苏则另有框架。

00:15:42.960 --> 00:15:56.448
During arrest, airway status and the resuscitation protocol determine coordination with compressions. Do not apply rescue-breathing numbers to a compression ratio or mix adult and pediatric procedures.
心搏骤停时，气道状态及复苏规程决定如何配合按压。不能把救援呼吸次数当成按压通气比例，也不能混用成人与儿科流程。

00:15:56.448 --> 00:16:10.080
In the school lab, state the named framework and then demonstrate an appropriate breath with feedback. A correct metronome rate cannot compensate for a leaking mask, an obstructed passage or excessive volume.
学校实训中，应先说清采用的框架，再演示有反馈的适当通气。节拍器次数正确，不能弥补漏气面罩、受阻通道或过大气量。

00:16:10.080 --> 00:16:22.680
The i-gel is a supraglottic device: it creates an interface around the laryngeal inlet rather than passing through the vocal cords. That distinction explains both its usefulness and its limits.
i-gel是声门上装置：它在喉入口周围建立通气界面，而不是穿过声带。这一区别同时解释了它的用途及局限。

00:16:22.680 --> 00:16:34.560
Its cuff is shaped to fit the anatomy and is not inflated with a syringe. Do not copy the inflation instructions for a King airway or an inflatable laryngeal mask onto this device.
它的套囊依靠解剖形状贴合，不需要用注射器充气。不能把King气道或充气型喉罩的充气步骤照搬过来。

00:16:34.560 --> 00:16:47.400
A gastric channel does not make the airway aspiration-proof. It also does not grant a PCP permission to insert a gastric tube; current local pharyngeal suction is a specifically limited procedure.
带有胃通道，不代表能完全防止误吸，也不授予PCP插胃管的权限；当前当地的咽部吸引属于受到专门限制的操作。

00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:57.888
The question is whether it safely improves airway management for this patient, not whether it is more advanced than a mask. Continue effective basic support while preparing it.
应问的是它能否安全改善该患者的气道管理，而不是它是否比面罩“更高级”。准备期间仍应维持有效基础支持。

00:16:57.888 --> 00:17:10.248
Current PR zero eight includes patients unable to protect the airway because of reduced consciousness. Outside cardiac arrest, its additional PCP training or sign-off conditions still apply.
当前PR08包括因意识下降而不能保护气道的患者；在非心搏骤停情况下，还须符合PCP额外训练或签核条件。

00:17:10.248 --> 00:17:27.648
Screen for a foreign body or pathological obstruction, active vomiting, caustic ingestion, relevant airway or neck trauma and inability to open the mouth. Anticipated high inspiratory pressure is also a warning about likely seal difficulty.
须筛查异物或病理性梗阻、活动性呕吐、腐蚀物摄入、相关气道或颈部伤及不能张口。预计吸气压很高，也提示可能难以密封。

00:17:27.648 --> 00:17:38.280
The current procedure requires confirming that the patient can be ventilated by BVM first. Do not use an i-gel as a blind attempt to bypass a suspected obstruction.
当前规程要求先确认能够用BVM通气。不能把i-gel当作盲目绕过疑似梗阻的尝试。

00:17:38.280 --> 00:17:51.120
State the backup before insertion: if placement is ineffective, return promptly to the effective basic method and call for appropriate help. That plan prevents fixation on a device that is failing.
置入前就要说出后备方案：若放置无效，应尽快恢复有效基础方法并取得适当支援。预先规划可避免执着于一个正在失败的器械。

00:17:51.120 --> 00:18:02.448
Use the weight range printed on the actual model together with anatomy. Adult size ranges overlap; that is a reason to assess fit, not a reason to choose by colour alone.
应结合实际型号印出的体重范围及解剖情况选择。成人尺寸范围有重叠，这说明需要评估贴合，不能只看颜色。

00:18:02.448 --> 00:18:14.304
Inspect the device, connector and channels and prepare the compatible ventilation circuit. Its protective cradle is packaging, never an introducer to be inserted into the mouth.
检查器械、接头及各通道，并备好相容通气回路。保护托架属于包装，绝不能当成要放入口腔的导入器。

00:18:14.304 --> 00:18:26.664
Apply the required thin water-based lubricant layer without leaving a lump that obstructs the airway opening. Keep contaminated fingers and damaged equipment out of the prepared patient-contact surface.
按要求涂薄层水性润滑剂，不能留下堵住气道开口的团块。准备好的患者接触面应避免被污染手指或破损器材污染。

00:18:26.664 --> 00:18:40.176
The manufacturer flash card is only a reminder and explicitly is not its full instructions for use. During supervised practice, identify the actual model and read its complete instructions before the station.
制造商速查卡仅作提示，并明确不是完整使用说明。督导训练前，应确认实际型号，并读该型号完整说明。

00:18:40.176 --> 00:18:49.944
Prepare everything before interrupting effective ventilation. Position the patient within injury precautions and open the mouth using the taught technique.
应在打断有效通气之前准备好所有物品。在伤情防护范围内摆位，并用所教方法开放口腔。

00:18:49.944 --> 00:19:03.480
For the described i-gel, the outlet faces the chin and the soft leading tip enters toward the hard palate. Advance with a continuous gentle movement along that contour until definite resistance.
所述i-gel的开口朝向下巴，柔软前端朝硬腭进入，沿该轮廓持续而轻柔推进，直至清楚阻力点。

00:19:03.480 --> 00:19:17.760
Do not repeatedly force or twist against resistance and do not inflate a nonexistent cuff. A failed attempt should trigger reoxygenation, reassessment and the actual attempt limits taught with the device.
不能遇阻后反复强推或扭转，也不能给不存在的充气套囊充气。尝试失败应促使重新氧合、复评，并遵守该装置实际所教的尝试限制。

00:19:17.760 --> 00:19:29.448
Connect the prepared ventilation circuit and check the patient immediately. Reaching a printed depth mark is not the final step; an effective breath is the next decisive observation.
连接已备好的通气回路后应立即检查患者。到达印出的深度标记不是最后一步，下一项决定性观察是一次有效通气。

00:19:29.448 --> 00:19:43.464
Confirm that breaths produce chest rise and air entry without a major leak. Listen and look for evidence of gastric inflation or ineffective delivery; a seated connector alone is not confirmation.
应确认通气产生胸廓起伏及气流进入，且没有显著漏气。观察并听取胃胀气或给入无效迹象，单凭接头已经插好不能确认成功。

00:19:43.464 --> 00:19:57.864
Use waveform capnography where available together with the clinical examination. A waveform adds evidence of exhaled gas but does not turn an SGA into a cuffed tracheal tube or guarantee protection from aspiration.
可用时应结合临床检查使用波形二氧化碳监测。波形增加呼出气体的证据，但不会使声门上装置变成套囊气管导管，也不保证防误吸。

00:19:57.864 --> 00:20:11.568
Secure the device with the supplied approved holder and reassess afterward. Current PR zero eight specifically says not to use a Thomas tube holder for this purpose, despite older materials showing different advice.
用随装置提供且获准的固定带固定，并在固定后复评。尽管旧资料说法不同，当前PR08明确不应为此使用Thomas导管固定器。

00:20:11.568 --> 00:20:25.152
After lifting, loading or moving the head, check the patient, device position, connections and waveform again. Fixation is intended to reduce displacement, not to eliminate the need to look for it.
抬起、装车或移动头部后，应再次检查患者、器械位置、接头及波形。固定是为了减少移位，不是为了免除移位检查。

00:20:25.152 --> 00:20:38.304
If the i-gel does not ventilate effectively, announce the failure rather than explaining it away as a low monitor reading. Check chest movement, seal, depth, connections and contamination.
i-gel不能有效通气时，应明确宣布失败，不能把它解释成“只是监测值低”。检查胸廓运动、密合、深度、接头及污染。

00:20:38.304 --> 00:20:50.328
Use only the gentle corrective maneuvers actually taught for that device. Forcing it deeper or increasing pressure indefinitely can worsen trauma, leakage and gastric inflation.
只能使用该装置实际所教的轻柔纠正动作。无限制加深或加压，可能加重创伤、漏气及胃胀气。

00:20:50.328 --> 00:21:05.472
When it is ineffective, return to the previously effective BVM method as required and request higher-level help. Continuing to ventilate through an unsuccessful interface is not perseverance; it is continued failed delivery.
装置无效时，应按需回到先前有效的BVM并请求更高级支援。继续通过失败界面通气，不叫坚持，而是持续无效给入。

00:21:05.472 --> 00:21:17.544
Also reconsider patient causes, including obstruction, bronchospasm and chest injury. A new airway device cannot correct every problem downstream in the lungs or circulation.
还应重新考虑患者原因，包括梗阻、支气管痉挛及胸伤。更换气道装置不能修复肺部或循环下游的所有问题。

00:21:17.544 --> 00:21:30.672
Current PR zero eight permits a modified pharyngeal suction approach through the i-gel port during cardiac arrest. This does not authorize gastric intubation or routine unrestricted suction through that port.
当前PR08允许在心搏骤停时，通过i-gel通道进行改良咽部吸引。这不授权插胃管，也不授权经该通道常规无限制吸引。

00:21:30.672 --> 00:21:44.952
PR twenty seven specifies a package-based measurement with an added two centimetres and a clear depth mark. The catheter must not advance past that mark. Learn the exact equipment and measurement on the supervised trainer.
PR27规定按包装测量后增加2厘米并作清楚深度标记，导管不能超过该标记。须在督导模型上学习实际器械及测量方法。

00:21:44.952 --> 00:22:01.176
The procedure stops suction when fluid clears or none appears after fifteen to twenty seconds. It specifies eighty millimetres of mercury, not generally above one hundred sixty; those are this procedure's limits, not universal suction settings.
该流程要求液体清除后，或15至20秒仍无液体出现时停止吸引；所列压力为80毫米汞柱，一般不超过160。这些是本流程的限制，不是通用吸引设置。

00:22:01.176 --> 00:22:14.520
Active vomiting with the i-gel in place requires removal and oral clearance rather than leaving it in place and continuously suctioning. Do not reinsert a displaced device while a catheter projects beyond its tip.
i-gel在位时发生活动性呕吐，应取出并清理口咽，不能原位持续吸引。导管伸出器械前端时，不能把已移位器械重新插回。

00:22:14.520 --> 00:22:26.592
A patient who begins to wake may no longer tolerate a supraglottic airway. Reassess breathing and airway protection rather than waiting for forceful biting, retching or self-removal.
患者开始苏醒后，可能不再耐受声门上装置。应重新评估呼吸及气道保护，不应等到用力咬合、干呕或自行拔除才行动。

00:22:26.592 --> 00:22:38.736
Prepare suction, a functioning bag and mask, oxygen and assistance before a planned removal. Use a position and removal method appropriate to the patient and current procedure.
计划取出前要准备吸引、可用球囊面罩、氧气及协助。按患者状态及当前规程选择体位和取出方法。

00:22:38.736 --> 00:22:50.496
Communicate with a cooperative patient and remove as actually trained; the i-gel has no cuff to deflate. Clear secretions and support breathing immediately if needed.
患者能合作时应先解释，再按实际训练方法取出；i-gel没有需要放气的套囊。按需清理分泌物并立即支持呼吸。

00:22:50.496 --> 00:23:01.032
Continue monitoring after removal. Improved alertness after reversal medication may be temporary, and the need for airway support can recur before handover.
取出后仍应持续监测。拮抗药后意识改善可能只是暂时，气道支持需求可能在交接前再次出现。

00:23:01.032 --> 00:23:16.608
An adult has a definite pulse, four shallow breaths per minute and a wet gurgle. Oxygen raises the displayed saturation to ninety-seven percent, but the first bagged breath produces almost no chest rise and an audible leak.
一名成人有明确脉搏，每分钟4次浅呼吸并伴湿性咕噜声。给氧后显示血氧97%，但第一次球囊通气几乎无胸廓起伏，还听到漏气。

00:23:16.608 --> 00:23:31.104
The correct interpretation is continued ventilatory failure, not a reassuring oxygen number. Clear obstructing fluid, reopen the airway and establish a two-hand seal with a second provider giving a controlled breath.
正确解释是通气衰竭仍在持续，而不是血氧数字令人放心。清除阻塞液体、重新开放气道，建立双手密合，由第二人给予受控通气。

00:23:31.104 --> 00:23:46.200
Now compare before and after: is there definite rise, improved air entry and useful exhaled carbon dioxide? If not, announce persistent failure, check the next link and request help without pausing all support.
再比较前后：是否有清楚起伏、更好气流及有意义的呼出二氧化碳？若没有，应宣布仍然失败、检查下一环，并在维持支持的同时求援。

00:23:46.200 --> 00:24:00.216
An SGA becomes a reasoned option only after indication, exclusions, actual authority and the prior-ventilation requirement are addressed. Giving an antidote does not replace these airway actions.
只有适应证、禁用情况、真实权限及先前能够BVM通气的要求都已处理后，声门上装置才成为有依据的选项。使用解毒药不能取代这些气道措施。

00:24:00.216 --> 00:24:11.520
Start the station by naming the immediate patient problem, checking equipment and assigning roles. The observer should be able to hear which findings justify the selected intervention.
训练站开始时应说清即时患者问题、检查器械并分工。观察者应能听出，哪些发现支持所选干预。

00:24:11.520 --> 00:24:23.592
Demonstrate opening and clearing the airway, selecting an appropriate adjunct and producing controlled chest rise with two-provider BVM. Explain what would make you stop or change the method.
演示开放并清理气道、选择合适辅助通气道，以及双人BVM产生受控胸廓起伏。说明出现什么情况会停止或更换方法。

00:24:23.592 --> 00:24:39.576
If the instructor provides an indicated SGA scenario, complete screening, preparation, insertion, confirmation and securement, then recheck after a simulated move. Do not announce success merely because insertion is finished.
若教师提供有适应证的声门上装置情境，应完成筛查、准备、置入、确认及固定，再于模拟搬动后复查。不能因为“插完了”就宣布成功。

00:24:39.576 --> 00:24:54.768
The instructor then introduces one failure. Identify the changed finding, correct the relevant link and demonstrate recovery of effective ventilation. Rehearse until the action and explanation both meet the actual school rubric.
随后由教师设置一种故障。找出变化的发现、纠正相关环节，并展示有效通气恢复。应练至动作与解释都达到学校实际评分要求。

00:24:54.768 --> 00:25:09.192
Report what the patient was doing before intervention, including pulse, respiratory effort, consciousness and airway contamination. Without a baseline, the receiver cannot judge the significance of the current numbers.
应报告干预前脉搏、呼吸努力、意识及气道污染。没有基线，接收者就难以判断当前数值的意义。

00:25:09.192 --> 00:25:22.008
State the actual positioning, suction, adjunct and airway device used, with relevant size, times and attempts. Document a failed attempt as failed, including the recovery method.
说明实际采用的摆位、吸引、辅助通气道及气道装置，并交代相关尺寸、时间及尝试。失败的尝试应如实记为失败，同时记录补救方法。

00:25:22.008 --> 00:25:35.328
Describe the response with observed chest movement, air entry, oxygenation and capnography trends. Distinguish an absent waveform from a low value and report any equipment limitation.
使用观察到的胸廓运动、气流、氧合及二氧化碳趋势描述反应。区分完全无波形与数值偏低，并报告器械限制。

00:25:35.328 --> 00:25:50.544
Finish with unresolved risks such as vomiting, recurrent sedation, difficult seal or displacement during movement, and tell the receiver which backup is ready. This closes the same assessment-support-reassessment loop with which the lesson began.
最后交代呕吐、再次镇静、难以密合或搬动移位等未解决风险，并说明已备何种后备支持。这就完成了本课开始时的评估、支持、复评闭环。
